<title>USA: Mass. drivers seen getting refunds on insurance.</title>
<headline>Mass. drivers seen getting refunds on insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Massachusetts drivers likely will get a discount in their 1997 insurance bills because a mathematician at the State Ratings Bureau discovered a flaw in the way insurance premiums are calculated.</p>
<p>Burt Feinberg said the miscalculation has cost policyholders a total of $200 million since 1992.</p>
<p>State officials have made arrangements to refund $50 million of that to drivers next year.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
